From: Paul Praschl <praschlpaul@g-p.at>
Date: Wed, 22 Jul 2026 12:45:38 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 021/117] dt-bindings: power: supply: add BQ27545 HDQ

The J172 BQ27545 is the single device on a Texas Instruments HDQ bus
synthesized by the T8010 UART. Describe the gauge as an HDQ child
instead of binding a private power-supply transport directly to serdev.

The binding carries the standard monitored-battery and optional
power-supplies relationships while leaving the physical UART framing to
the HDQ bus binding. This describes hardware only; the existing BQ27xxx
HDQ family driver and the UART W1 master provide the runtime
implementation.

Signed-off-by: Paul Praschl <praschlpaul@g-p.at>

Orchard-replay-of: 90076404666f8110d134fee5307e63de7cbfc6d4
---
